hadiths[73]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1426","The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) with reference to some other isnads."
"1427","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: I had a complaint about Nasur. I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the prayer, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \Pray while standing. If you cannot do this"","" then sit down. If you cannot do this"","" then pay the Pahlavi.\"""""""
"1428","The same tradition is narrated along with another tradition, however, the name of the disease, basoor, is quoted in it."
"1429","Sayyidna Ya'li bin Umayyah narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we reached a place that was narrow, the sky was above us and the valley below us. It was time for prayer. While living, he prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1430","Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktoum Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: He said, O Messenger of Allah, there is no one to accompany me, who stays with me all the time, while there are also drains and trees between me and the mosque, so is there room for me to pray in my house?"
"1431","Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (PBUH) and he slept until the sun came up. The Prophet (PBUH) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (RA)."
"1432","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person has performed one rak'at of the morning prayer, he should perform the second rak'at while the sun rises."
"1433","A narrator named Hammam narrates: Qatadah was asked about a person who had performed one rakat of the morning prayer and then the sun came out, then Qatadah said: This saying of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1434","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: He who has performed one rak'ah of morning prayer and then the sun rises during that time, he should complete his prayer."
"1435","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A person who has performed one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer and the sun rises during that time, then that person should perform the Fajr prayer."
"1436","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Whoever has not performed the two Rak'ats of Fajr until the sun rises"","" he should perform them both.\"""""""
"1437","Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and all the people fell asleep at the time of the Fajr prayer. They woke up due to the heat of the sun. When the sun rose a little and became bright, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the muezzin. Wasallam performed the Fajr prayer (as a judgment)."
"1438","Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1439","Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: Once he came (to the mosque) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the Fajr prayer. He said, I did not pay them before Fajr (i.e. these are the two sunnahs of Fajr), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent and did not say anything."
"1440","Sayyiduna Qays bin Amr (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) saw a man who was offering two rak'ahs after the Fajr prayer. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired whether the morning prayer is offered twice. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent."
"1441","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to participate in an expedition (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these words are:) to Syria. When the last part of the night came, we camped (and slept). We could not wake up until the heat of the sun woke us up. We traveled for a while until the sun rose a little, then the people did their needs, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal to give the Adhan: Then we prayed two rak'ats, then he said Iqamah under the command of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the morning prayer. We said: O Prophet of Allah! Shall we not make up for it tomorrow in its time? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: Will Allah forbid you people from usury, and accept it from you?"
"1442","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a sermon (after which the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith) in which these words are: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no extravagance in sleeping for the person who does not perform the prayer until the time of the next prayer arrives."
"1443","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If there is any worldly work of yours, it is your business, and if there is a religious matter, it will come to me. (after) pay or pay on time the next day."
"1444","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about people falling asleep during the prayer, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no Tafreet in falling asleep, the Tafreet is in waking up. The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) heard me narrating this hadith and said to me: O young man, remember the hadith you are narrating because I too have heard this hadith from the mouth of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1445","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission, in which there is a similar story, but it contains these words: We said: Shall we not pay it tomorrow? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you from usury and will accept it himself."
"1446","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: (After that, he narrated a tradition similar to this, which contains these words): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you from usury and He will accept it from you."
"1447","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people of Makkah! Do not shorten the prayer by less than four barads (travelling a distance) equal to the distance from Makkah to Isfan."
"1448","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once we traveled with the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) stayed for seventeen days, during which time the Prophet (PBUH) continued to offer short prayers. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas says: When we are travelers and stay for thirteen days, we shorten the prayer; if we stay longer than that, we offer the full prayer."
"1449","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We stayed with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for seventeen days in one place during a journey, during which time we continued to offer short prayers. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We will offer short prayers for seventeen days; if we have to stay longer than that, we will offer complete prayers."
"1450","Kareeb narrates: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Shall I tell you about the way the Prophet (PBUH) prayed during a journey? We answered: Yes! So he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in his residence and the sun was setting (i.e. it was noon), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers together before leaving for the journey, and when the sun had not set when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present (in the house) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to leave, he would leave. Then when it was Asr time, at that time he would stop his journey and perform Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time. Likewise, if it was Maghrib time in the residence of the Prophet (peace be upon him), he would perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time, and if it was not Maghrib time, he would leave and perform these two prayers together at the time of Isha prayer. The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1451","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was the custom of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when the sun went down, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and when he left before the sun set, he would postpone these two prayers and even the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform these two prayers at the time of the Asr prayer."
"1452","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was encamped somewhere and the sun had already set, he would not leave until he had performed the Asr prayer, and if he had left before sunset, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would offer both prayers at the time of the Asr prayer."
"1453","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to leave after the sun had set, he (may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him) would offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and if he had to leave before that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would postpone the Zuhr prayer until Asr time."
"1454","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers together during a journey, he used to postpone the Zuhr prayer until the early Asr time came (so he used to perform both prayers together at that time)."
"1455","Ibn Shihab narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to set out on a journey before the sun set, he would set out until Asr time began, then he would halt and offer these two prayers together."
"1456","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, so he would postpone the Zuhr prayer until the early time of Asr began, and then he would perform these two prayers together."
"1457","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar came to Makkah and he was informed of the illness of his wife Safiyya bint Abu Ubaid, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar accelerated his journey. When the sun set, one of his companions said: It is time for prayer, but Sayyidna Abdullah remained silent. Ibn Umm (may God be pleased with him) continued walking until dusk fell, so he halted and called for prayer. Here the Nishapuri narrator has quoted a different word, the following words are agreed upon by the narrators who say: Sayyiduna Abdullah stood up and offered Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time. They used to perform their prayers regardless of the direction of the Suri. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) told these people: What the Prophet (PBUH) used to do in the same way."
"1458","Salim narrates: When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) was informed of his (wife) Safiyya's illness, he began to travel quickly, then he narrated a tradition similar to this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in which these words are: \Shortly after sunset\"". A narrator named Ibn Wahib followed him."""""
"1459","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would set out for a journey, he would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and when he started to leave before that, he would postpone the Zuhr prayer and perform the Asr prayer early and perform these two prayers together."
"1460","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) had to travel fast, he used to perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time. A narrator has also quoted the words of, till the fourth night."
"1461","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"1462","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk (this was the practice of the Holy Prophet) when the sun had set before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, he would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left before the sun set, he would delay the Zuhr prayer until he stopped for the Asr prayer. If the sun set before leaving, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time, and if he left before sunset, he would postpone the Maghrib prayer, then stop for Isha and perform these two prayers together."
"1463","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but its chain of transmission is somewhat different."
"1464","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was the custom of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk (from encampment during the journey) when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left before the sun set, he would postpone the Zuhr prayer until the time of Asr when he offered both of them together, and when he left after the sun had set, he would offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers together and then leave. In the same way, when he left before Maghrib, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to postpone the Maghrib prayer, until he offered it together with the Isha prayer, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left after the sunset, he would quickly offer the Isha prayer and perform it with the Maghrib prayer. Imam Abu Dawud has stated this: This hadith has been narrated only by a narrator named Qatadah."
"1465","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1466","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was informed of the illness of his wife Safiyyah. He was traveling at that time. He accelerated his speed when the sun set and asked him to pray. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had to do something, he used to do it in the same way."
"1467","Nafee narrates a similar hadith on the authority of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), but it contains these words: He encamped before twilight and offered the Maghrib prayer, and then he waited until twilight fell, then he offered the Isha prayer."
"1468","Narrated Nafi: I set out with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, he was on his way to his land. He stopped at a place on the way. A man came to him and told him (his wife) Safia bint Abu Ubaid is in a critical condition and I think you will not be able to reach her (before her death). We were traveling until the sun set. I was closely related to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He used to pray with great regularity. I said: It is time for prayer. He did not pay attention to me and continued walking as he had been going before until when it was the end of twilight, he stopped and offered Maghrib prayer. Fascinated, he told us that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to hurry in a matter, he used to do the same."
"1469","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"1470","Nafee narrated: Once we were coming from Makkah with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, until on the way he was told about the serious illness of his wife Safiyyah, so he sped up the journey. It was his custom to get down and offer the Maghrib prayer at the same time as the sun set, but that night it did not happen. He offered the prayer, then when the twilight had set, he stood up and offered the Isha prayer, then he turned towards us and told us, what we used to do with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1471","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1472","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Jaafar (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray standing up, except in the case of fear of drowning. Imam Dar Qutni narrates: What is meant is that they should pray while standing in the Kushi."
"1473","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Ja'far bin Abu Talib to Abyssinia, he said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we pray in a boat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Pray standing in it"","" unless you are afraid of drowning.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition"","" Husain bin Alwan"","" is obsolete."""""
"1474","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about praying in a boat, and he said: “It is to be prayed standing up, but if you are afraid of drowning (the ruling is different)."
"1475","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Whoever performs two prayers at the same time without any excuse will be guilty of a major sin. Shaykh says: The narrator named Hansh is Abu Ali Rahbi and it is abandoned."
"1476","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was traveling and he had to perform the Nafl prayer, he used to turn his camel towards the Qiblah and then say Takbeer."
"1477","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was on a journey and had to perform the Nafl prayer, he used to face the Qiblah and then say Takbeer."
"1478","Sayyidina Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was on a journey and had to perform the Nafl prayer, he (PBUH) would turn his camel towards the Qiblah, then say Takbeer and then start performing the prayer, regardless of the direction in which his stirrups were facing."
"1479","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) sent me on some errand, and when I returned, you were on your horse. I greeted you, but you did not answer me. Then I saw you bowing and prostrating with gestures, so I stood aside. Then he said to me, \What did you do with your errand?\"" I said that I have done such and such. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not respond to you because I was praying."""""
"1480","Mahmood bin Labaid narrates: Sayyidna Asayd bin Hudair complained of ``Irq al-Nisa''. He was our Imam."
"1481","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this as a hadeeth: One who prays while sitting gets half the reward of one who prays while standing, except for the person who sits cross-legged."
"1482","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) sitting and praying."
"1483","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a problem, he ordered Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to lead the people in prayer, then the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace) felt better, so he came and sat by Sayyidna Abu Bakr’s side. study"
"1484","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this about Sayyidna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt better, so he walked (into the mosque) supported by two men. Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) came and sat by Sayyidna Abu Bakr's side. He started reciting from the place where Sayyidna Abu Bakr left off."
"1485","Imam Shaabi narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that no one should lead while sitting."
"1486","Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about praying with a bow, so he said, \Take off the horn and pray while wearing a bow.\"""""""
"1487","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates: \At the time of every prayer"","" take adornment\"". He says: This means praying with shoes on. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing shoes"","" then he took them off"","" so the people also took off their shoes. The people said"","" \""We saw you take off your shoes"","" so we took them off.\"""""""
"1488","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to give food to our Imam during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1489","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whoever gives a morsel to the Imam, he has spoken, (meaning his prayer will be broken). The narrator of this hadith is Muhammad bin Salem."
"1490","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This is the word (says the narrator) that is, giving food to the Imam."
"1491","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the Imam asks you for something to eat, feed him (i.e. give him a bite if he forgets)."
"1492","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching us the prayer, he started reciting a surah, he left out a verse from it. When he finished the prayer, I said, \O Messenger of Allah"","" may God's prayers and peace be upon him"","" has such and such a verse been abrogated?\"""""""
"1493","Sayyidina Anas (RA) narrates: The Companions of the Prophet (PBUH) used to give each other morsels during prayer."
"1494","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If one dirham of blood is applied, that prayer will be repeated. Some other narrators have not disagreed in narrating it."
"1495","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when there is blood on the cloth as much as one dirham, then the cloth will be washed and the prayer will be performed again."
"1496","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and one of its narrators is obsolete."
"1497","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the Imam returns the salam, you return the salam to the right and to the left, and after that you do not turn to any part of your prayer."
"1498","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The prayer that you lead with the Imam will be your first prayer, and you should perform the recitation that has been completed before. Saeed bin Musayb also has the same opinion as Sayedna Ali."
